{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013pB9dsTNuzQCQHRncJqcnm","type":"tool_result","content":"393:## 18. The device opt-in maximum is not the kernel's maximum, and the safety margin that failed a passing gate\n428:## 19. The variance is BETWEEN checkpoint loads, not within them — 0.6 % vs 5.7 %\n471:## 20. A gate that does not compile is a gate that passes by never running (ladder 1.5, 2026-08-20)\n519:## 21. dprof reads a saving 15–20 % low, so it attributes but does not ratchet (ladder 1.5)\n542:## 22. `tau` reproduced to four decimals; `tok/s` on the same protocol did not — and the promotion gate keys on the second one (ladder 2.2, 2026-08-20)\n606:## 23. A drift control that failed — and the agent that was contaminating its own arms (ladder 3.1, 2026-08-20)\n655:## 24. The base-AR window times the governor, not the engine — and it is 21 % (ladder 3.1, 2026-08-20)\n692:## 25. A unit gate that stops six times short of the regime it is quoted about (ladder 1.9, 2026-08-20)\n721:## 26. A field that was never computed compares equal, and equal reads as exonerated (ladder 1.9)\n749:## 27. `build/decode` and `dsv4-server` do not share a prefill, and a bit-exactness result on one says nothing about the other (ladder 1.9)\n770:## 28. A tuning default that was a regression at its own design point, and the mechanism story that was wrong (ladder 1.7, 2026-08-20)\n814:## 29. A dprof mark that timed another stream's work, and reported it as a 3.2x swing in a GEMM (ladder 1.8, 2026-08-20)\n=== context-scaling\n6:## The claim this page retires\n25:## Two mechanisms made it invisible, and both were structural\n42:## The attribution\n64:## What this changes\n80:## The rule this produces\n93:## Status — 1.0 is done, and the term it removed came off the measured slope\n117:## Status — 1.2 is done too, and it found a term the profile could not see\n144:## Status — 1.3 did not move this term, and that is the entry\n163:## Status — 1.5 is done, and